    "description": "The v3 schema lets a definitions array carry, beside structured content, a two-element pair [uninflectedTerm, [inflectionRule, ...]] recording the rule chain that produces an inflected surface. Jitendex emits it on redirects -- [\"\uff2e\u97ff\", [\"redirected from \uff2e\u97ff\"]] -- 131789 times in rev 2026.02.05. parse_term_bank stores the whole definitions array verbatim, so a generic walker recursed into the pair and rendered raw row metadata as if it were a gloss; the entry came out as a redirect plus the literal text 'redirected from \uff2e\u97ff'. This pins that the pair is metadata and never reaches the rendered senses. Payload is trimmed from a real Jitendex redirect row (term_bank_1, seq -1000130). mobile_mirror is null -- PC-hosted formatting defect, not a mobile parity surface.",
